window.docContents[161].resolve({"/3___-General-results-of-representation-theory/3___8___-The-Krull-Schmidt-theorem/Section-3___8___-The-Krull-Schmidt-theorem-___-heading/#Chapter3___Introduction_to_3___8___heading-1":{"contents":"","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t3. General results of representation theory\t3.8. The Krull-Schmidt theorem\tSection 3.8: The Krull-Schmidt theorem — heading","header":"3.8. The Krull-Schmidt theorem","id":"/3___-General-results-of-representation-theory/3___8___-The-Krull-Schmidt-theorem/Section-3___8___-The-Krull-Schmidt-theorem-___-heading/#Chapter3___Introduction_to_3___8___heading-1"},"/4___-Representations-of-finite-groups___-Basic-results/4___5___-Orthogonality-of-characters/Orthogonality-of-characters___-inner-product-equals-dim-Hom/#Chapter4___Theorem4___5___1":{"contents":"Theorem 4.5.1. For any representations V, W\n\n(\\chi_V, \\chi_W) = \\dim \\mathrm{Hom}_G(W, V),\n\nand\n\n(\\chi_V, \\chi_W) = \\begin{cases} 1, & \\text{if } V \\cong W, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if } V \\not\\cong W \\end{cases}\n\nif V, W are irreducible.\n\nProof. By the definition\n\n(\\chi_V, \\chi_W) = \\frac{1}{|G|} \\sum_{g \\in G} \\chi_V(g)\\overline{\\chi_W(g)} = \\frac{1}{|G|} \\sum_{g \\in G} \\chi_V(g)\\chi_{W^*}(g)\n\n= \\frac{1}{|G|} \\sum_{g \\in G} \\chi_{V \\otimes W^*}(g) = \\operatorname{Tr}|_{V \\otimes W^*}(P),\n\nwhere P = \\frac{1}{|G|} \\sum_{g \\in G} g \\in Z(\\mathbb{C}[G]). (Here Z(\\mathbb{C}[G]) denotes the center of \\mathbb{C}[G].) If X is an irreducible representation of G, then\n\nP|_X = \\begin{cases} \\mathrm{Id} & \\text{if } X = \\mathbb{C}, \\\\ 0, & X \\neq \\mathbb{C}. \\end{cases}\n\nTherefore, for any representation X the operator P|_X is the G-invariant projector onto the subspace X^G of G-invariants in X. Thus,\n\n\\operatorname{Tr}|_{V \\otimes W^*}(P) = \\dim \\mathrm{Hom}_G(\\mathbb{C}, V \\otimes W^*)\n\n= \\dim(V \\otimes W^*)^G = \\dim \\mathrm{Hom}_G(W, V).\n\n\\square\n\n\n\n","context":"Introduction to Representation Theory\t4. Representations of finite groups: Basic results\t4.5. Orthogonality of characters\tOrthogonality of characters: inner product equals dim Hom","header":"Orthogonality of characters: inner product equals dim Hom","id":"/4___-Representations-of-finite-groups___-Basic-results/4___5___-Orthogonality-of-characters/Orthogonality-of-characters___-inner-product-equals-dim-Hom/#Chapter4___Theorem4___5___1"}});
